# Project Overview & Development Guide

This document provides a high-level overview of the `xsoulspace.github.io` project, its architecture, and the guiding principles for its development. It is intended to be a starting point for any developer or AI agent working on the codebase.

## 1. Core Idea & Vision

This project is the official portfolio website for **xsoulspace.dev**, an indie studio focused on creating excellent products through quality, iteration, and open-source principles. The website serves to showcase the studio's work across several categories: Apps, Games, Utilities, and foundational open-source libraries.

The design philosophy, as outlined in `docs/plan_v2.md`, emphasizes a simple yet epic and unique user experience with distinct, purpose-driven layouts for each section.

## 2. Technology Stack

The project is built on a modern Vue.js 3 ecosystem:

- **Framework:** [Vue 3](https://vuejs.org/) (Composition API)
- **Build Tool:** [Vite](https://vitejs.dev/)
- **Language:** [TypeScript](https://www.typescriptlang.org/)
- **Routing:** [Vue Router 4](https://router.vuejs.org/)
- **Internationalization (i18n):** [Vue I18n](https://vue-i18n.intlify.dev/)
- **SEO & Meta Management:** [VueUse Head](https://vueuse.org/integrations/head/)
- **Styling:** Global CSS variables (`src/assets/main.css`) and scoped styles. [SASS](https://sass-lang.com/) is available.
- **Data Parsing:** [YAML](https://yaml.org/) for parsing content files.

## 3. Project Architecture

The codebase is organized in a standard, scalable structure within the `src/` directory.

- **`main.ts`**: The application entry point. Initializes Vue, Router, and i18n.
- **`App.vue`**: The root Vue component.
- **`assets/`**: Contains global styles (`main.css`), static images, icons, and fonts.
- **`components/`**: Shared Vue components, organized by layout (`layout/`), page sections (`sections/`), and general UI elements (`ui/`).
- **`composables/`**: Reusable Vue Composition API functions (e.g., `useSEO.ts`, `useDesignSystem.ts`).
- **`data/`**: Holds content for the website. This is transitioning from static `.ts` files to language-specific `.yaml` files (e.g., `data/en/apps.yaml`).
- **`locales/`**: Contains translation files (`en.ts`, `ru.ts`) and the i18n setup logic.
- **`pages/`**: Top-level components that correspond to application routes.
- **`router/`**: Defines the application's routes in `index.ts`.
- **`services/`**: Contains business logic, such as data fetching and parsing (`projectService.ts`).
- **`types/`**: TypeScript type definitions, primarily for data models (`project.ts`).

### Rendering Flow

1.  The app is mounted in `main.ts`.
2.  `App.vue` renders `AppLayout.vue`.
3.  `AppLayout.vue` provides the global structure (e.g., header, footer) and a `<router-view>` outlet.
4.  Vue Router dynamically renders the appropriate page component from `src/pages/` inside the `<router-view>`.

## 4. Guiding Principles & Implementation Plans

This section summarizes the development plan derived from `docs/plan_v2.md`.

### Main Page (`Index.vue`)

- **Layout:** A full-width, multi-row layout. Each row is a large, clickable link to a main section.
- **Component:** `src/components/sections/HomeNavigation.vue`.

### Project Showcase Pages (`Apps.vue`, `Games.vue`, `Utilities.vue`)

- **Layout:** A two-column design utilizing a **CSS Scroll Snap** pattern.
- **Left Column:** Contains descriptive text for a list of projects.
- **Right Column:** Contains sticky media elements (images, GIFs, videos) that change as the user scrolls through the projects.
- **Component:** `src/pages/ProjectShowcasePage.vue` is the template for these pages.

### Foundation Page (`Foundation.vue`)

- **Layout:** A two-column layout tailored for developers.
- **Left Column:** A condensed, clickable list of foundation packages/libraries.
- **Right Column:** Displays a code example and a short description for the selected package.

### Ethics Page (`Ethics.vue`)

- **Layout:** A two-part page.
- **Part 1:** A **Bento Grid** to visually represent the studio's core principles and values.
- **Part 2:** A letter explaining the philosophy behind these ethics.

## 5. Key Development Tasks

- **Data Migration:** Transition all project data from the static files in `src/data/*.ts` to the new localized YAML files in `src/data/en/` and `src/data/ru/`. The `projectService.ts` should be updated to load and serve this data.
- **Page Implementation:** The component files for `ProjectShowcasePage.vue`, `Foundation.vue`, and `Ethics.vue` exist but are mostly placeholders. They need to be implemented according to the layouts described above.
- **Responsiveness:** Ensure all page layouts are fully responsive and provide an excellent experience on both mobile and desktop devices.
- **SEO:** Continue using the `useSEO` composable on all pages to provide relevant titles and meta descriptions.

